e": "en"}], "synonyms": ["सञ्जृम्भ्"], "synonyms_slp1": ["saYjfmB"]}], "sanjf": [{"id": "saMjF", "headword": "संजॄ", "headword_slp1": "saMjF", "fold": "sanjf", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "सं-√ 1. जॄ P. -जीर्यति, to become old together, MaitrS.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "सं-√ 2. जॄ Ā. -जरते, to sound together, sound forth, RV.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["सञ्जॄ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["saYjF"]}], "sanjYa": [{"id": "saMjYa", "headword": "संज्ञ", "headword_slp1": "saMjYa", "fold": "sanjYa", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "1. सं-ज्ञ mfn. (fr. सं + 1. ज्ञ = ज्ञु; cf. 1. प्र-ज्ञ) knock-kneed, L.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "2. सं-ज्ञ mfn. (ifc. for सं-ज्ञा, e.g. लब्ध-संज्ञ, ‘one who has recovered consciousness’, MBh.; -ता f. ‘recovery of c˚’, Veṇīs.)", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "सं-ज्ञ n. a yellow fragrant wood, yellow sanders, L.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}, {"id": "saMjYA", "headword": "संज्ञा", "headword_slp1": "saMjYA", "fold": "sanjYa", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "सं-√ ज्ञा P. Ā. -जानाति, -जानीते, (Ā.) to agree together, be of the same opinion, be in harmony with (loc.; accord. to Pāṇ. ii, 3, 22, also instr. or acc.), RV.; AV.; VS.; ŚBr.;\n (Ā.) to obey (dat.), AitBr.;\n (Ā.) to appoint, assign, intend (for any purpose), destine, ib.;\n (only ind.p. -ज्ञाय) to direct, order, command, Hariv.;\nto acknowledge, recognize, own, Pāṇ. i, 3, 46, Sch.;\n (P.) to acknowledge or claim as one's own, take possession of SaddhP.;\n (P.) to think of, recollect sorrowfully (with acc. or gen.), Pāṇ.; Vop.;\n Ā. to know well, understand, R.;\nto watch for, Bhaṭṭ. :\nCaus. -ज्ञापयति or -ज्ञपयति, ˚ते, to cause to be of the same opinion or agree together, AV.; AitBr.;\nto cause to acquiesce or agree in (euphemistically said of a sacrificial victim, which ought not to be led forcibly to its death but made to resign itself), ŚBr.; GṛŚrS.; MBh.; BhP.;\nto appease, satisfy, MBh.; Kālid.;\nto make to be understood or known, cause to understand, ŚBr.;\nto make signs to (acc.), communicate or make anything known by signs, Mṛcch.; Hcar.;\nto command, enjoin, instruct, Hariv.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "सं-ज्ञा (आ), f., see below", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "सं-ज्ञा॑ f. (ifc. f(आ). ) agreement, mutual understanding, harmony, TBr.; ŚBr.; Kathās.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "consciousness, clear knowledge or understanding or notion or conception, ŚBr. &c. &c.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "a sign, token, signal, gesture (with the hand, eyes &c.; संज्ञाम्-√ कृ or दा, ‘to give a signal’), MBh.; Kāv. &c.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "direction (in अ-कृतस्˚, ‘one who has received no d˚’), MBh.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "a track, footstep, BhP.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "a name, appellation, title, technical term (ifc. = ‘called, named’), Nir.; Mn.; MBh. &c.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "(in gram.) the name of anything thought of as standing by itself, any noun having a special meaning (संज्ञायाम् therefore denotes ‘[used] in some peculiar sense rather than in its strictly etymological meaning’ e.g. as a proper name), Pāṇ. i, 1, 34; 2, 53 &c.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "a technical expression in grammar (see -सूत्र)", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "(with Buddhists) perception (one of the 5 Skandhas q.v.), Dharmas. 22; MWB. 109", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "N. of the Gāyatrī (q.v.), L.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "of a partic. high number, Buddh.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "N. of a daughter of Tvaṣṭṛ or Viśva-karman (the wife of the Sun and mother of Manu, Yama and Yamī), Hariv.; Pur.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "sanjYu": [{"id": "saMjYu", "headword": "संज्ञु", "headword_slp1": "saMjYu", "fold": "sanjYu", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "सं-ज्ञ